  "id": "electronics.analog-circuits.timer-circuits",
  "name": "Timer Circuits",
  "level": "process",
  "parent": "electronics.analog-circuits",
  "description": "Design pedagogy for the 555 timer IC (the most ubiquitous integrated circuit ever made) and its modes of operation: astable free-running multivibrator, monostable one-shot pulse generator, and voltage-controlled PWM. Covers the internal architecture (two comparators, RS flip-flop, discharge transistor, 1/3-2/3 V_CC resistor divider), the canonical timing formulas, and the canonical applications — LED flasher, time-delay relay, tone generator, and servo PWM.",
  "timeline": "Years 25-40",
